+---
+id: dl-004-applymergepatch-semantics-immutable-own-properties-only-null-deletes
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyMergePatch semantics: immutable, own properties only, null deletes"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+# Context
+
+RFC 7386 defines the merge algorithm but leaves implementation choices open: mutation, prototype
+safety, and inherited names. `applyPatch` (dl-002) already set conventions for these.
+
+# Decision
+
+- Follow the RFC algorithm exactly: a non-object patch replaces the target, an object patch merges,
+  `null` deletes a member, arrays are replaced whole.
+- Never mutate inputs and share no structure with them (deep clone), as `applyPatch` does.
+- Address only own members; set members with `defineProperty` so `__proto__` stays plain data.
+- Never throw: any JSON value is a valid patch.
+
+# Consequences
+
+- A `null` in a target cannot be set by a merge patch (inherent to RFC 7386).
+- Callers get a fresh value on each call, at the cost of a copy.
